  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Sri Sujal Kanti Saha vs State Of West Bengal on 17 November, 2022 In The High Court At Calcutta 17-11-2022 Criminal Revisional Jurisdiction Subha Item no.32 Crr 1916 of 2021 Ct no.34 Sri Sujal Kanti Saha -versus- State of West Bengal.",
    "facts": "However, the learned A.C.J.M, Tehatta, Nadia rejected such an application. I find that the subject matter 18,000 kg of cumin was seized on 19th August, 2020. A sample from the said cumin was sent for analysis on 20th August, 2020 to the Food Analyst by the Deputy Chief Medical Officer of Health, Nadia. The samples referred therein do match with the report of the Public Analyst, which was submitted, opining the same to be unsafe for human consumption.",
    "arguments": "Mr. Chatterjee, learned advocate appearing for the petitioner prays for return of the seized 18,000 kg of black cumin which were seized in the instant case by the Investigating Authorities.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "Mr. Chatterjee, learned advocate appearing for the petitioner prays for return of the seized 18,000 kg of black cumin which were seized in the instant case by the Investigating Authorities.",
